  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "On the stone lotus island in the River of Time, Fang Yuan compares Earth’s butterfly effect with what rebirth does in the Gu world and concludes the ink effect explains those influences better.",
      "chapters": [
        1754
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_river_of_time",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He frames rebirth as bringing a will from the downstream to the upstream through Spring Autumn Cicada, then fusing with himself at a point in time. Because this world’s time is unique and absolute with no parallel dimensions, the downstream remains as it was after he died, while after rebirth he is like a drop of ink in clear river water: as he changes events and people, the ink spreads and dyes the river a different color. He can change things readily because fate Gu is incomplete and because he is an otherworldly demon not bound by fate, whereas a native such as Red Lotus Demon Venerable finds many outcomes pulled back toward their original route. Otherworldly demons are a huge blob of ink; native Gu Immortals are only short-lived ripples under fate Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        1754
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rebirth-as-ink",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_spring_autumn_cicada",
        "gu_fate_gu",
        "char_red_lotus_demon_venerable",
        "sys_otherworldly_demon",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "With his strength and influence, the ink effect of that rebirth becomes much more significant.",
      "chapters": [
        1756
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "expanding-rebirth-pressure",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He sometimes repeats prior-life actions on purpose to keep the ink from expanding in ways that would cost his advantage.",
      "chapters": [
        1767
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "expanding-rebirth-pressure",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A later chapter titled for the ink effect notes that since rebirth the effect has given him many benefits and also caused problems.",
      "chapters": [
        1777
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "benefits-and-problems",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
